{"op": "task_created", "id": "project-skeleton", "title": "Project skeleton and layout", "description": "Create examples/expr-parser layout: src/ for implementation, include/expr/ for headers, tests/ for test sources. Add .gitignore ignoring build artifacts (expr, expr_tests, *.o). Add an empty src/main.cpp that returns 0 (replaced by the REPL task later).", "acceptance": ["src/main.cpp exists and compiles to a runnable binary", "include/expr/ and tests/ directories exist", ".gitignore excludes build artifacts"], "files": ["src/main.cpp", "include/expr/.gitkeep", "tests/.gitkeep", ".gitignore"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 1, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "build-system", "title": "Makefile build/test/clean", "description": "Write Makefile: CXX=g++, CXXFLAGS=-std=c++14 -Wall -Wextra. Targets: all (build src/*.cpp into ./expr), test (build and run ./expr_tests from tests/*.cpp + src/*.cpp, exit nonzero on failure), clean (remove expr, expr_tests, *.o). No cmake required.", "acceptance": ["make builds ./expr", "make test runs the test binary", "make clean removes artifacts"], "files": ["Makefile"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 2, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "token-def", "title": "Token kind enum and Token struct", "description": "include/expr/token.h: enum class TokenKind { Number, Identifier, Plus, Minus, Star, Slash, Caret, Percent, LParen, RParen, Comma, End, Error }; struct Token { TokenKind kind; std::string text; size_t pos; }; plus const char* token_kind_name(TokenKind) for diagnostics.", "acceptance": ["token.h compiles standalone", "token_kind_name returns a readable string for every kind"], "files": ["include/expr/token.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 3, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "error-report", "title": "ParseError and EvalError with positions", "description": "include/expr/error.h: struct ParseError { std::string message; size_t pos; }; struct EvalError { std::string message; }; both derive from std::exception. Helper std::string render_error(const std::string& source, const ParseError& e) producing 'message\\n<source>\\n  ^ (at column N)' so errors point at the offending character.", "acceptance": ["ParseError carries message and pos", "render_error includes the caret line and column number"], "files": ["include/expr/error.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 4, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "lexer", "title": "Lexer with numbers, identifiers, operators, errors", "description": "src/lexer.cpp + include/expr/lexer.h: std::vector<Token> lex(const std::string& src). Skip whitespace. Numbers: integers, decimals (1.5), exponent notation (1e3, 2.5e-2). Identifiers [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*. Operators: + - * / ^ % ( ) ,. Unknown character -> TokenKind::Error token with position (do not throw; the parser decides). Input ends with an End token at src.size().", "acceptance": ["lex(\"2+3*4\") yields Number Plus Number Star Number End", "lex(\"1e3\") yields a single Number token with text \"1e3\"", "lex(\"2$3\") yields an Error token at the position of '$'"], "files": ["src/lexer.cpp", "include/expr/lexer.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 5, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "lexer-tests", "title": "Lexer unit tests", "description": "tests/lexer_tests.cpp: table-driven checks. Cover: basic ops, decimals, exponent notation (1e3, 2.5e-2), identifiers, mixed whitespace, unknown char error, empty input (End only). Print 'lexer tests: N passed' on success; exit nonzero on any failure.", "acceptance": ["all lexer table cases pass", "test binary reports a clear pass/fail summary"], "files": ["tests/lexer_tests.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 6, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "ast-def", "title": "AST node definitions", "description": "include/expr/ast.h: struct Node { enum Kind { Number, Variable, Unary, Binary, Call } kind; double number; std::string name; char op; std::shared_ptr<Node> left, right; std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Node>> args; }; plus factory helpers: make_number(double), make_variable(std::string), make_unary(char, node), make_binary(char, l, r), make_call(name, args). Use std::shared_ptr (C++14; no std::variant on GCC 6).", "acceptance": ["ast.h compiles standalone", "factory helpers construct the right node kinds"], "files": ["include/expr/ast.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 7, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "parser", "title": "Precedence-climbing parser", "description": "src/parser.cpp + include/expr/parser.h: std::shared_ptr<Node> parse(const std::vector<Token>& tokens) (throws ParseError). Precedence: lowest + - (left assoc), then * / % (left assoc), then ^ (RIGHT assoc), unary - and + bind tighter than * / but looser than ^ (so -2^2 == -(2^2) == -4). Parentheses group. Identifier followed by '(' is a function call with comma-separated arguments (allow empty call? no - at least one arg). Trailing tokens after a complete expression are a ParseError. ')' with no matching '(' is a ParseError. Track current token index; report positions from tokens.", "acceptance": ["parse(\"2+3*4\") gives Binary(+ 2 (* 3 4))", "parse(\"2^3^2\") gives Binary(^ 2 (^ 3 2)) — right associative", "parse(\"-2^2\") is Unary(- (^ 2 2))", "parse(\"sqrt(4)\") is Call(sqrt [4])", "dangling ')' or trailing garbage throws ParseError with position"], "files": ["src/parser.cpp", "include/expr/parser.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 8, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "parser-tests", "title": "Parser unit tests", "description": "tests/parser_tests.cpp: build token vectors via lex and check AST shapes. Cases: precedence (2+3*4), left associativity (10-3-2 == (10-3)-2), right associativity (2^3^2), unary minus on numbers and on parens (-(2+3)), function calls (sin(x), pow(2,3)), parenthesized grouping, error cases (\")\", \"2+\", \"2 3\" trailing, missing closing paren). Use a small AST-shape printer for assertions. Exit nonzero on any failure.", "acceptance": ["all precedence/associativity/call cases pass", "every error case throws ParseError"], "files": ["tests/parser_tests.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 9, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "context", "title": "Variable context and builtin functions", "description": "include/expr/context.h + src/context.cpp: class Context { double& operator[](std::string); bool has(name) const; }; builtins table: sin cos tan asin acos atan sqrt cbrt abs log log10 exp floor ceil round; constants pi and e seeded. Table maps name -> double(*)(double).", "acceptance": ["context supports set/get/has", "pi and e are pre-seeded", "builtin function table contains at least 12 math functions"], "files": ["include/expr/context.h", "src/context.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 10, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "evaluator", "title": "Evaluator over the AST", "description": "src/evaluator.cpp + include/expr/evaluator.h: double eval(const std::shared_ptr<Node>&, const Context&) (throws EvalError). Number -> value. Variable -> lookup, unknown variable throws EvalError. Unary -/+ -> negate/identity. Binary: + - * / % ^ with double math (fmod for %, pow for ^). Division by zero throws EvalError('division by zero'). Call: look up builtin, unknown function throws EvalError, call with the argument evaluated. No arity>1 builtins needed except pow handled as n-ary? Keep single-arg builtins; pow(2,3) support: special-case pow with two args in evaluator.", "acceptance": ["eval(2+2) == 4", "eval(2^3^2) == 512", "eval(1/0) throws EvalError", "eval(sqrt(9)) == 3 with builtin table", "eval(unknown_var) throws EvalError", "pow(2,3) == 8"], "files": ["src/evaluator.cpp", "include/expr/evaluator.h"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 11, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "evaluator-tests", "title": "Evaluator pipeline tests", "description": "tests/evaluator_tests.cpp: full pipeline lex->parse->eval. Cases: 2+2, 10-3-2, 3*4+5, 2^10, 2^3^2, sqrt(9), abs(-4), sin(0), pi*2, x*2 with Context x=21 -> 42, 1/0 throws, 5%2 == 1, 2+3*4 == 14, -2^2 == -4, pow(2,3) == 8. Exit nonzero on any failure.", "acceptance": ["all pipeline cases evaluate to expected values", "error cases throw EvalError"], "files": ["tests/evaluator_tests.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 12, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "print-ast", "title": "AST pretty printer", "description": "include/expr/print.h + src/print.cpp: std::string print_ast(const std::shared_ptr<Node>&) producing S-expression-ish output: Number(n), Variable(name), Unary(op expr), Binary(op l r), Call(name args...). Used by parser tests and the REPL debug command.", "acceptance": ["print_ast(Binary(+ 2 (* 3 4))) == \"(+ 2 (* 3 4))\"", "print_ast handles Call and Unary nodes"], "files": ["include/expr/print.h", "src/print.cpp"], "priority": "low", "notes": [], "seq": 13, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "repl", "title": "REPL and single-shot CLI", "description": "Replace src/main.cpp with the real CLI. Modes: (a) argv expression mode: ./expr \"2+3\" prints the result and exits 0; parse/eval errors print the rendered error to stderr and exit 1. (b) interactive REPL when no args: prompt '> ', read a line, lex/parse/eval, print the result (with up to 12 significant digits), print rendered errors and continue; 'quit' or EOF exits 0. Hidden command ':ast <expr>' prints the AST via print_ast.", "acceptance": ["./expr \"2+3\" prints 5 and exits 0", "./expr \"1/0\" prints error to stderr and exits 1", "./expr \"2+\" prints a positioned parse error and exits 1", "REPL evaluates and exits on quit/EOF"], "files": ["src/main.cpp"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 14, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "cli-tests", "title": "CLI end-to-end tests", "description": "tests/cli_tests.cpp: a driver that runs the built ./expr binary with system() or fork/exec: asserts \"2+3\" -> stdout \"5\", \"10-3-2\" -> \"5\", \"1/0\" -> nonzero exit + stderr contains 'division by zero', \"2+\" -> nonzero exit + stderr contains 'column', \"pi\" -> 3.14159...; also REPL via piped stdin (\"2+3\\nquit\\n\" -> \"5\"). Print 'cli tests: N passed'.", "acceptance": ["single-shot mode outputs correct values and exit codes", "REPL mode evaluates piped input", "error messages include positions"], "files": ["tests/cli_tests.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 15, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "edge-cases", "title": "Edge-case stress tests", "description": "tests/edge_cases.cpp: deep nesting (50 nested parens), long chains (1+2+...+100 == 5050), whitespace-heavy input, empty input error, unary chains (---5 == -5), 5*-3, 1e-3, scientific with negative exponent, % with negatives (fmod semantics), sqrt(-1) -> NaN handling (evaluate, don't crash), very large numbers (1e308), function calls in expressions (sin(0)+cos(0) == 1).", "acceptance": ["all stress cases produce correct values or clean errors", "no crashes on pathological input"], "files": ["tests/edge_cases.cpp"], "priority": "medium", "notes": [], "seq": 16, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
{"op": "task_created", "id": "readme", "title": "Proof README (front door)", "description": "Write README.md per proofs/PROOF_SPEC.md section 4.1, in order: What was built; Why this proof exists (claims C1 and C3 with one sentence each); Final architecture (subsystems with dependency arrows); Commands (make, ./expr, make test); Reproduce (Forge version, proposal id prop_expr_parser_001); Artifact index; Behavior notes; Lessons learned. List Claim IDs C1, C3.", "acceptance": ["all 8 required sections present in order", "C1 and C3 claims listed with support sentences", "commands section works from a clean checkout"], "files": ["README.md"], "priority": "high", "notes": [], "seq": 17, "ts": "2026-08-06T10:59:07+00:00", "v": 1}
